WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.080
Nora had been to see her aunt

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.400
who was expecting a baby.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.640
She was curious to know whether it

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.260
would be a baby boy or a baby girl.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.560
But how can this be found?

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.140
How is the sex of a child determined ?

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:19.020
And is it the same for other animals as well?

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.600
Let's find out.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.580
Sex determination is carried out in various types.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.640
The two major types that we will focus on

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.360
are the genotypic sex determination

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.460
and the environmental sex determination.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.100
Let's begin with the first type.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.700
That is the genotypic method.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.000
In this type,

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.700
the sex of a child is determined

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.060
by the sex chromosomes.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.160
We know what sex chromosomes are.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.060
In humans, for example,

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.400
the last pair is the sex chromosomes,

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:01.440
while the first 22 pairs are called autosomes.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:02.940
Similarly,

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:05.020
in many other organisms

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:06.960
the sex chromosomes help to decide

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.280
the sex of an individual.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.040
Let's take an example of mammals.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.500
In most of them,

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:14.720
including humans

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:21.000
the sex of a child is determined by the sex chromosomes namely 'X' and 'Y'.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.160
We know that in humans,

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.420
individuals with both 'X' chromosomes are females

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:32.100
while those with '1 X' and' 1 Y' are males.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:36.340
This is one type of genotypic sex determination.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:39.520
Now, let's take the case of birds.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.100
It is similar to the case of humans.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.120
But only that their system is reversed.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.120
In the case of birds, the females have

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.980
two different sex chromosomes,

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.740
while males have both similar chromosomes.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.800
We use the letters 'Z' and 'W'

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.760
to represent the chromosomes in them

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.220
These letters are used just in order to

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.860
avoid any confusion

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.360
with our human chromosomes.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.960
So a female is the one with 'ZW'

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.120
and a male is the one with

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.960
'ZZ' set of sex chromosomes.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.760
So the sex of the birds' offspring

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:19.060
is dependent on females.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.580
If the mother gives her Z chromosome,

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.920
then it will be a male, with “ZZ” chromosomes,

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:28.180
while if the mother gives a 'W' chromosome,

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:32.440
then it will be a female with 'ZW' chromosomes.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:36.500
So just like in the case of humans in birds as well,

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.140
the sex of the offspring

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:41.180
is determined by the sex chromosomes.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.560
Wasn't this interesting ?

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:45.840
Now let's understand the other types of

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.680
genotypic sex determination

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:49.960
in the upcoming part.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.060
Humans and birds

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.100
have an amazing genotypic sex determination method.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:01.980
The presence of a different sex chromosome

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.440
plays the vital role in determining the

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.720
sex of the offsprings.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:11.640
Now let's discuss the third type of genotypic sex determination.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.220
In this case, just like humans

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:17.920
here we have the sex chromosomes 'x' and 'y'.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.240
But the presence of a 'Y' chromosome

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:23.500
has got nothing to do with the sex of the child.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:25.760
In fact, the sex chromosomes

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:28.000
are not the only factors instrumental

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.500
in deciding the sex of the child.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:34.240
It is the ratio of the sex chromosomes to the autosomes

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.480
that decides the offspring to be a male or a female.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:41.500
And which organisms exhibit this pattern of

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.480
Sex determination?

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.140
One example is the common fruit fly

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.760
or the Drosophila melanogaster.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.100
But what exactly is this ratio system?

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.780
It's the ratio of sex chromosomes to the autosomes

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.500
that determine the sex of the offsprings.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:03:59.500
For example,

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.040
when a fly has 'two x' chromosomes

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.180
and two sets of autosomes ,

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.540
then the ratio obtained will be two is to two,

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.300
which is one!

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:13.240
The flies with this ratio of 1 are females.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:16.800
A Fly with the ratio of 0.5 is male.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.220
So in case a fly, has one X and one Y

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.620
and two sets of autosomes,

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:27.560
then the ratio will be 1 is to 2 making the fly a male

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.320
Now tell me,

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:32.180
what if a fly has 3 sex chromosomes,

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.740
XXY and two sets of autosomes,

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.740
will it be a male or a female?

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.500
Give it a shot!

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.120
Let's crack this together.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:45.780
If we calculate aptly,

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:47.960
then there are two x chromosomes

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.980
and two sets of autosomes

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:54.060
Thus, the ratio obtained is 2 is to 2, that's one.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:56.940
So this fly will be a female.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:59.220
The presence of the Y chromosome

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:01.680
does not affect the sex of this fly.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:04.600
It's the ratio of the X chromosomes

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:08.100
to the autosomes that determines the sex.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:11.020
Now let's talk about one more interesting type of

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:12.360
sex determination

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:14.580
that makes use of genes.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:18.360
This system is called the haplodiploid system

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.540
Can you guess what the system could be?

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:24.140
Well, let me help you.

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.000
The haplodiploid system is the one

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:30.160
in which the males are haploid as they develop from

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:32.260
unfertilized eggs.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:33.900
And females are diploid

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.920
as they develop from fertilized eggs.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.700
This system in which males are haploids

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:42.420
and females are diploids is called the

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:45.040
haplodiploid system.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:47.420
This system is predominantly found in the

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:51.120
lower members of the animal kingdom like insects.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:56.020
Bees, wasps and ants exhibit Haplodiploidy.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.560
There are a few more types of genotypic

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:01.000
sex determination prevailing in nature.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.240
But for now,

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:04.300
we will deviate towards the next type

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:05.380
of sex determination,

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.760
which is environmental sex determination.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:12.300
Let's learn about that in the next part.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:17.540
What will happen to water

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:22.480
if kept at 0 degree Celsius or at 100 degrees Celsius?

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:26.700
At 0 degrees the water will freeze to form ice,

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:30.220
while at 100 degrees it will start to boil.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:33.340
But... Do you think temperature effects only

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:35.100
nonliving objects?

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:37.520
Nope, it has a huge impact

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:40.440
on the life of living beings as well.

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:43.420
Apart from regulating various body systems,

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.740
it has a huge influence on several

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:48.500
important processes of nature.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.060
Take sex determination, for example

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:53.400
In certain animals,

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:55.020
the sex of the offsprings

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:57.000
is dependent on the temperature at

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:59.500
which the eggs are incubated.

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:01.680
We note that sex determination

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:04.280
occurs in two major ways.

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.520
One is genotypic sex determination

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:10.580
and the second is environmental sex determination.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.480
So temperature dependent sex determination

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:16.020
is a type of the latter form.

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:19.400
Let's look at this type in detail.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:20.920
To begin with

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.480
the sex of the offsprings in some animals

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:26.620
is dependent on environmental factors.

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:28.120
The first type is

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:31.260
temperature dependent sex determination.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:34.880
In some reptiles like crocodiles and alligators

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.420
the sex of the offspring depends on the

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:40.240
temperature at which the eggs incubate.

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:43.960
If the temperature is high then the offspring is female,

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.340
while if it's a low temperature

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:49.480
then the offspring is a male.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:53.460
Same is the case for certain turtle species.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:57.660
If their eggs are incubated above 32 degrees Celsius

00:07:57.960 --> 00:07:59.940
then all develop as females,

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:03.400
while if incubated below 28 degrees Celsius

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:06.600
then all develop as males.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:09.080
Apart from temperature dependency

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.820
what other environmental factors determine the

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:13.460
sex of an offspring?

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:16.280
Well location is one thing.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:20.860
Yes, you heard me right... but location of what?

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:22.420
To understand this

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:25.580
let's take the example of the green spoon worm.

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:27.760
There are two possibilities

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:30.580
where these free-floating larvae can land.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.880
If the larvae land on the bare ocean floor

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.120
then they turn out to be females

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:37.780
and on the other hand

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:39.980
if they land on the body of a female

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:43.920
then that makes the larvae turn into a male.

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:48.100
This is how location helps determine the larvae sex.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:52.320
Isn't this type of sex determination interesting ?

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:54.520
To revise in a nutshell

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:57.140
sex of offsprings in various animals

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:00.980
is determined by two major types

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:03.060
one is the genotypic method

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:06.680
and the other is using environmental factors.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.120
The genotypic method involves the sex chromosomes

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:13.220
that determine the sex of the offsprings.

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:17.100
Just like the XX and the XY system in humans

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:21.560
or the ZZ and the ZW system found in birds.

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:23.700
Another type in this category

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:27.020
is the ratio of sex chromosomes to the autosomes

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:29.320
which is seen in lower animals

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:32.200
like Drosophila melanogaster.

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:35.160
The second type of sex domination system

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:38.160
is the environmental system.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:42.180
Animals, like crocodiles alligators and turtles

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:45.880
exhibit the temperature-dependent sex determination,

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:49.140
while lower animals like the green spoon worm,

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:53.360
exhibit the location dependent sex determination.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:56.460
So this was about the sex determination system

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:59.180
found in various organisms.

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:02.680
To know more fascinating things in genetics

